==English==

===Etymology===
{{blend|calf|ankle}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|æŋkəl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang|pejorative}} An obese or otherwise swollen ankle that blends into the calf without clear demarcation.
#: '''2001''' &mdash; Hey, all l’m saying is she’s got '''cankles''', for God’s sake. ''What?'' '''Cankles'''! She’s got no ankles. It’s like the calf merged with the foot, cut out the middleman. &mdash; [[w:Shallow Hal|Shallow Hal]]
#: '''2004''' &mdash; The “'''cankle'''” (or the appearance of not having an ankle, but the calf of the leg just connecting to the foot) is a look that many women have and most could live without. &mdash; Jeff Smith, ''Posing for Portrait Photography: A Head-to-Toe Guide''
#: '''2005''' &mdash; They’d pass me magazines and ask how my '''cankle''' recovery was progressing.  They’re ankles, not '''cankles'''.  I don’t have '''cankles'''! &mdash; Franz Wisner, ''Honeymoon with my Brother''
#: '''2008''' &mdash; Stop saying I have '''cankles'''! &mdash; Amy Poeler as Hillary Clinton, ''Saturday Night Live'' (13 September 2008)

